{
  "an8.22:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 8.22 ",
  "an8.22:0.2": "3. Householders ",
  "an8.22:0.3": "With Uggata of Elephant Village ",
  "an8.22:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying in the land of the Vajjis at Elephant Village. ",
  "an8.22:1.2": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants: ",
  "an8.22:1.3": "“Mendicants, you should remember the householder Uggata of Elephant Village as someone who has eight amazing and incredible qualities.” ",
  "an8.22:1.4": "That is what the Buddha said. ",
  "an8.22:1.5": "When he had spoken, the Holy One rose from his seat and entered his dwelling. ",
  "an8.22:2.1": "Then a certain mendicant robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to the home of the householder Uggata of Elephant Village, where he sat down on the seat spread out. ",
  "an8.22:2.2": "Then Uggata of Elephant Village went up to that mendicant, bowed, and sat down to one side. The mendicant said to him: ",
  "an8.22:2.3": "“Householder, the Buddha declared that you have eight amazing and incredible qualities. ",
  "an8.22:2.4": "What are the eight qualities that he spoke of?” ",
  "an8.22:3.1": "“Sir, I don’t know ",
  "an8.22:3.2": "what eight amazing and incredible qualities the Buddha was referring to. ",
  "an8.22:3.3": "But these eight amazing and incredible qualities are found in me. ",
  "an8.22:3.4": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "an8.22:3.5": "“Yes, householder,” replied the mendicant. ",
  "an8.22:3.6": "Uggata of Elephant Village 